hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1249","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb and Abu Sa’id Al-Ashjaj told us, saying: Abu Khaled told us, Husayn Al-Mukhtab told us, and Bundar told us, Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein, H., Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, meaning Ibn Zurayi, Husayn Al-Mu’allim narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The prayer of a sleeping person is half the prayer of one sitting.” Abu Bakr said: I knew before that the Arabs give the name of the sleeper to the one who is lying down and to the sleeper whose reason is lost due to sleep, but he only wanted The Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “And the prayer of the sleeper,” he who lies down does not lose his mind through sleep, since he who loses his mind through sleep does not understand prayer. At the time of the disappearance of reason"
